+## 6. Scripted path
+
+The scripts in `.dev/issues/442/scripts/` run sections 1 to 5 for an agent, under the owner authorization in section 4.2. Their working state, logs and screens are under `/tmp/ob` (override with `OB`). Run them in this order (the order of section 3.1):
+
+| Order | Script | What it does |
+|---|---|---|
+| 1 | `setup.sh` | Sections 1.1 to 1.3: preconditions, baselines, the isolated HOME, the probe and the repositories. |
+| 2 | `session-a.sh` | Session A (section 2.1), through the driver. |
+| 3 | `session-a2.sh` | Session A2 (section 2.1b, item 7). |
+| 4 | `evidence.sh all` | Drafts `.dev/issues/442/observation-results.md` and copies logs, screens and state to the package's `artifacts/ob-logs/` only when a secret scan finds nothing. |
+| 5 | `setup-github.sh` | Section 1.4: the four disposable issues, the claim session, the worktrees and the probe settings. |
+| 6 | `session-gov.sh b`, `c`, `d`, `e` | Sessions B to E (section 2.2). Every subcommand refuses unless OB-H1 item 5 is PASS in the results file, and `d` and `e` also need item 1 (section 3.3). |
+| 7 | `evidence.sh all` | Run again after each session. A part that needs a person stays `pending` until `evidence.sh --reading <u20\|retry-f7-f8\|ac7> <text> [screen file]` records it. |
+| 8 | `cleanup.sh` | Section 5.2. Without `--apply` it prints the plan and deletes nothing. `--apply` refuses while the results file is missing, and step 7 refuses while `ob-logs/` is missing or a new store entry remains. |
+
+The helpers are `lib.sh`, `driver.sh` and `driver-helpers.sh`. The tests are `lib-selftest.sh`, `setup-selftest.sh`, `driver-selftest.sh`, `session-a-selftest.sh`, `setup-github-selftest.sh`, `session-gov-selftest.sh`, `evidence-selftest.sh`, `cleanup-selftest.sh` and `runbook-selftest.sh`, all run by `selftest.sh`. The tests use stub commands in temporary directories and do not start a live session. The prompt files are in `scripts/prompts/`.
+
+Two stops need the owner or the driving agent:
+
+- `NEEDS_INPUT <screen file>`: the driver found a permission or login dialog on a session's screen. If it was there before a prompt, nothing was sent; if it appeared while the driver waited for the turn to end, the prompt had already been sent, so do not send it again. `session-a.sh`, `session-a2.sh` and `session-gov.sh` print this stop as a `PENDING` line (`screen=<file>`, or `reason=needs-input`), and `setup-github.sh` prints `NEEDS_INPUT claim <T> screen=<file>`. Read the saved screen. Answer with `driver.sh answer <name> <key> <reason>` only when the dialog is about a target of this run's disposable set, and answer nothing else. The answer is logged.
+- `BLOCKED login-isolated-home` (exit 3 of `setup.sh`): `claude -p` failed in the isolated HOME, usually because it could not authenticate. That is the owner's decision. The scripts never copy credential files.
+
+A `PENDING` line from a session script means the script stopped without recording that step; the line gives the reason, and some of these lines name a saved screen file. A gated skip (session `d` or `e` refused by the stop rules) is a valid recorded outcome: record it, run no further governed session, and go to the cleanup.
